<title>BELGIUM: Koramic group net H1 1996 profit up 18 pct.</title>
<headline>Koramic group net H1 1996 profit up 18 pct.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-09-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to June 30, 1996</p>
<p>(in millions of Belgian francs unless stated)</p>
<p>    Group net profit		   502  vs   427</p>
<p>    Cons sales/turnover (bln)   14.67   vs 3.96</p>
<p>NOTE - Koramic Building Products NV, formerly known as Terca Brick Industries NV, is a Belgian building products group said some figures were not directly comparable with those of 1995 following its link with Austria's Wienerberger group and an associated restructuring earlier this year.  </p>
<p>    Cons operating profit	 1,559  vs   973</p>
<p>    Amortization of goodwill	  4  vs    34</p>
<p>    Cons current profit	   1,172  vs   747</p>
<p>    Current cash flow	     2,425  vs 1,176</p>
<p>    Extraordinary loss		 32  vs    20</p>
<p>    Cons net profit		   788  vs   426</p>
<p>    Group net cash flow	   1,269  vs   789</p>
<p>In a statement, Koramic said forecasting second half results was difficult because of economic uncertainty in many of the countries where it operates.</p>
<p>&quot;However, we hope that activities in the majority of divisions of our group progress more favourably in the second half than in the first,&quot; Koramic said.</p>
<p>-- Nick Antonovics, Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6817, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
